      "writtenOn": "2024-04-23T07:02:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok I understood. So this patch actually attempts to change the behavior of `hfp_hal_interface::get_wbs_supported` (DBus method `is_wbs_supported`), which is how we check the WBS capability in Tauto. Note that it\u0027s actually not used by CRAS.\n\nLooked into an AC7265 WBS test log CRAS correctly disabled MSBC so I believe no users are affected: `dbus in: org.chromium.bluetooth.BluetoothMedia: StartScoCall: \"E4:5F:01:5D:3E:2A\", \"false\", \"MSBC | LC3\"`\n\nIn the current design I\u0027d say whether or not WBS is available is decided by CRAS, not Floss[*]. So I guess we should remove the wbs check in Tauto and block the tests in a chipset-based manner.\n\n*: WBS supported \u003d\u003d HW supported | SW supported; HW supported \u003d\u003d kCodecMsbc \u0026 CRAS has PCM; SW supported \u003d\u003d quirk is set. Floss doesn\u0027t know whether CRAS has PCM so the final decision is always made by CRAS.",
      "parentUuid": "365c3776_e677611b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 114,
